BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260519T042241Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52613522460195
DTSTART:20260421T163000Z
DTEND:20260421T173000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the TraCS Data Science Lab as we talk about the experience
  of implementing healthcare AI. Healthcare AI is generating unprecedented 
 investment and regulatory momentum — yet the vast majority of AI pilots 
 never reach frontline care.\n\n \n\nThis seminar cuts through the hype to 
 examine why\, tracing the full clinical AI deployment pipeline from model 
 development through post-deployment monitoring and the overlooked governan
 ce\, workflow\, and implementation challenges that derail efforts. Using r
 eal-world case studies — including the widely-deployed Epic Sepsis Model
  — we'll explore how dataset shift\, alert fatigue\, and clinician behav
 ior consistently outweigh algorithmic performance as barriers to impact.\n
 \n \n\nWhether you're a clinician\, informaticist\, or health system leade
 r\, this talk will reframe how you think about AI in medicine: the future 
 won't be decided by better models\, but by better implementation.\n\n \n\n
 Register\n\n \n\nSpeaker:\nDavid Friedlander\, MD\, MPH\nAssistant Profess
 or\, Department of Urology\nTDSL Faculty Scholar\, TraCS Data Science Lab\
 nUNC School of Medicine\n\n \n\n---\n\nSeminars in the NC TraCS Data Scien
 ce Lab Seminar Series cover a range of topics related to health care data 
 science\, clinical data\, data engineering\, and working in these areas at
  UNC-Chapel Hill. These hybrid seminars are usually held monthly on the th
 ird Tuesday of each month from 12:30-1:30 p.m. in the NC TraCS suite on th
 e 2nd floor of Brinkhous-Bullitt or via Zoom.
GEO:35.905771;-79.051242
LOCATION:Brinkhous-Bullitt Building\, 219
SUMMARY:TraCS Data Science Lab: Healthcare AI Seminar
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/healthcare-ai
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260519T042241Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52620082466361
DTSTART:20260421T220000Z
DTEND:20260421T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:While social media was initially proposed as a way to foster co
 nnection and belonging to the next generation\, there is growing concern t
 hat it may be doing just the opposite – increasing loneliness while gett
 ing youth “hooked” by algorithm driven design features. At a time when
  adolescent’s social lives and brain development are remarkably dynamic\
 , social media has the potential to have long term impacts\, for better or
  worse. In this talk Drs. Angelica Carranza and Jimmy Capella will discuss
  the current state of research on social media’s impacts on development\
 , highlighting the risks and opportunities of the online social world. Joi
 n us on Tuesday\, April 21\, from 6:00 – 7:00 PM at the Chapel Hill Publ
 ic Library. We will serve light refreshments during the talk. This event i
 s made possible with the support of UNC Carolina Seminars.
GEO:35.932032;-79.035632
LOCATION:Chapel Hill Public Library\, Meeting Room A
SUMMARY:UNC Postdoctoral Association's Research Cafe
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/unc-postdoctoral-associations-
 research-cafe-6283
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
