DTSTART:20260422T160000Z
DTEND:20260422T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Using the philosophy that “those who are happy at home perfor
 m better on the job\,” this workshop was developed for those who feel bu
 rdened with too many responsibilities and without enough time for personal
  enjoyment. This workshop will help participants explore and define home r
 esponsibilities\, identify career requirements and prioritize leisure time
 . The resulting better balance will help achieve more in one’s career an
 d at home.\n\n \n\nWorkshop Objectives\nAt the end of this workshop\, you 
 will be able to:\nIdentify the components of a balanced lifestyle\n• Des
 cribe the concept of balance\n• Identify what is out of balance in your 
 life\n• Describe how notions of balance have changed over time in your l
 ife and historically\n• Identify the relationship between stress and bal
 ance\nIdentify and explore the balance between home responsibilities\, car
 eer requirements\nand leisure activities\n• Describe how to create your 
 own balance diagram\n• Identify the right questions to achieve balance\n
 • Describe the role of prioritization\, limit setting and time managemen
 t to balancing work and life\n• Identify tips and suggestions on how to 
 achieve balance\n• Identify a personalized action plan to achieve balanc
 e in your life\n\n \n\nClick on Carolina Talent registration link and sele
 ct the “Request” button to automatically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Balancing Work and Life
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/balancing-work-and-life-8344
