DESCRIPTION:The UNC–KCL Classical Reception Colloquium is an annual event
 \, established in May 2025 with funds from the UNC–KCL Collaboration Gra
 nt. Alternating between KCL and UNC\, the colloquium brings together gradu
 ate students and faculty scholars from both institutions to explore new di
 rections in reception theory and practice. Transhistorical and transnation
 al in its scope\, this year’s classical reception colloquium showcases c
 ross-disciplinary perspectives on the afterlife of ancient visual and lite
 rary culture in a wide variety of media. Participants share and develop th
 eir research on the ways in which the diverse visual cultures of the ancie
 nt world influenced art\, philosophy\, literature\, and culture in subsequ
 ent periods.
GEO:35.913407;-79.052875
LOCATION:Hyde Hall\, University Room
SUMMARY:UNC-KCL Colloquium in Classical Reception
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/unc-kcl-colloquium-in-classica
 l-reception
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260519T042241Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51375426939308
DTSTART:20260429T160000Z
DTEND:20260429T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:The problem with most attempts to adopt stress-management or se
 lf-care routines is that they require time\, effort and planning. The real
 ity for many people who have stressful jobs is that they are too physicall
 y exhausted and mentally depleted by the end of the day to initiate activi
 ties commonly recommended to reduce stress in their lives. The trick is to
  intervene via multiple “micro-moments” of relaxation or mindful pract
 ices which only take 15 to 60 seconds. These moments of relaxation help br
 ing stress levels down during the workday and interrupt the steady escalat
 ion of stress that creates physical and mental exhaustion. Also addressed:
  simple winding-down routines that can end the day in a calming\, mindful 
 way.\n\n \n\nWorkshop Objectives\nThis training will help you:\n• Descri
 be how stress escalates through the day and leads to exhaustion\n• Consi
 der whether your present stress reduction habits may be adding to your ove
 rall stress\n• Understand how simple short moments of relaxation through
 out the day can permit you reduce stress and\nconserve energy\n• Practic
 e brief mindful moments of relaxation and learn how to integrate these mom
 ents into your workday\n• Understand the value of winding-down routines 
 that foster a sense of safety and personal control.\n\n \n\nClick on Carol
 ina Talent registration link and select the “Request” button to automa
 tically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Relaxation “Micro-Moments” and Winding Down Techniques
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/relaxation-micro-moments-and-w
 inding-down-techniques-7099
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
