DESCRIPTION:Calling all bird brains: celebrate International Migratory Bird
  Day at Morehead Planetarium and Science Center! 🐣\n\nIn this special e
 dition of Saturday Science Sparks\, you'll get the chance to meet the scie
 ntists of UNC’s Sockman Lab and explore the wonders of winged migration.
  Try the tools of a bird researcher as you explore why some birds fly daun
 ting distances\, and help the Sockman scientists uncover how the Earth’s
  seasons impact a bird’s journey.\n\n🎟️ Included with paid admissio
 n and located in the Morehead Planetarium Launch Lab.\n\nSCHEDULE \n10:00 
 am to 12:00 pm\n1:00 pm to 3:00 pm\n\nPlease note: there will be a midday 
 break.\n\nABOUT SATURDAY SCIENCE SPARKS\nMORE is happening at Morehead thi
 s year! New for 2026\, Saturday Science Sparks offers Morehead guests a cl
 oser encounter with current science. Covering topics like astronomy\, the 
 physics of juggling\, and computer science\, this program collaborates wit
 h community partners and academic clubs\, bringing you up-close experience
 s in the exciting world of STEAM. Saturday Science Sparks is open to the p
 ublic and included in admission.
GEO:35.913753;-79.050409
LOCATION:Morehead Planetarium and Science Center
SUMMARY:Saturday Science Sparks: The Science of Migration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/saturday-science-sparks-the-sc
 ience-of-migration
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
END:VEVENT
