DESCRIPTION:Local newspapers were once an indispensable part of Americans
 ’ news diets\, sustained by subscriptions\, advertisers\, and the commit
 ments of reporters\, editors\, and publishers.  The news ecosystem has cha
 nged dramatically in the past two decades as newspapers have been replaced
  by social media.  What are the implications? And what does it take to bui
 ld and sustain local news outlets today? \n\n \n\nRegister Here\n\n \n\nFe
 aturing\n\n\n\nMarisa Porto\, Knight Chair in Local News and Sustainabilit
 y\, Hussman School of Journalism \n\n\n\nErica Perel\, Operations Director
 \, Tiny News Collective \n\n \n\nDetails\n\nDATE & TIME: Saturday\, May 2\
 , 2026 | 11:00 am-2:30 pm\n\nCOST: $55 in person\; $30 virtual viewing | $
 15 discount for Carolina Alumni members\n\nLOCATION: Drakeford Library Com
 plex\, Carrboro
GEO:35.909417;-79.072001
LOCATION:Drakeford Library Complex
SUMMARY:The Latest News on Local News
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-latest-news-on-local-news
CATEGORIES:Lectures
CATEGORIES:Meetings and Conferences
