DESCRIPTION:What unites Americans? Being vaccinated! More of us get vaccine
 s than use smartphones\, own cars\, or watch reality TV. In May’s Caroli
 na Science Cafe\, Professor of Health Behavior Dr. Melissa B. Gilkey will 
 share research on the parent advocates and clinical champions who make US 
 vaccination programs possible. In addition\, we will discuss ways to suppo
 rt these programs to ensure that everyone has the opportunity to protect t
 heir families from measles\, human papillomavirus (HPV) cancers\, and othe
 r vaccine-preventable diseases.\n\n \n\n🎟️ Free and open to adults\n\
 n🍴 Light appetizers available for attendees\n\n🍻 Drinks available fo
 r purchase\n\n📍Hosted at Haw River Tap & Table in Carrboro.\n\n \n\nPre
 sented by Morehead Planetarium and Science Center\, Carolina Science Cafes
  explore science topics making national and international headlines\, offe
 ring adults the chance to meet the experts behind the work. Join Morehead 
 on the first Tuesday of every month!
GEO:35.910154;-79.068833
LOCATION:Haw River Tap & Table
SUMMARY:Carolina Science Cafe: US Vaccination Programs
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/carolina-science-cafe-us-vacci
 nation-programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
