UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52638316612227
DTSTART:20260508T130000Z
DTEND:20260508T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Each year\, graduating seniors celebrate by taking photos at Ca
 rolina landmarks. One of the most popular sites is Wilson Library’s Fear
 rington Reading Room. \n\n \n\nOn May 8\, the Fearrington Reading Room wil
 l be open during business hours for students who want to stop by and take 
 pictures there. Here’s what you need to know: \n\n \n\nBring your own ph
 otographer. \nThe Library will provide the space\, but you’ll need a cam
 era and someone to take your picture. Flash photography is ONLY allowed on
  May 8.  \nUsing flash in Wilson Library on other days is strictly prohibi
 ted\, as camera flashes can set off building alarms. Stay to your right.  
 \nWhen you enter the reading room\, head to the right. The left side of th
 e room is reserved for studying without disruption. Be respectful of other
  students. \nAlthough the right side of Fearrington will be open for photo
 graphy\, the entire space is still available for studying. Please be respe
 ctful of your peers while taking photos. Have fun! \nThe University Librar
 y is excited to be part of your Carolina experience and your graduation ce
 lebrations! Tag us in your photos @UNCLibrary.
GEO:35.90984;-79.050769
LOCATION:Wilson Library \, Fearrington Reading Room
SUMMARY:Wilson Photo Day
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/wilson-photo-day-5772
END:VEVENT
