UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52752797248322
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260515
DESCRIPTION:Ancestral Frequencies explores heritage and identity as mutable
  and shaped through fragments of memory\, migration\, ritual\, and imagina
 tion. This exhibition features the work of the graduating artists in the C
 lass of 2026 earning a Master of Fine Arts in studio art: Rojano Mohammadz
 adeh\, CJ Murphy\, Michelle Lisa Polissaint\, Iris Moyan Wang\, and Wendy 
 Yamilett. This cohort represents a wide breadth of cultural heritage and a
 rtistic media. In their art\, mythologies\, spiritual practices\, and hist
 orical narratives appear as living systems that shift as they move across 
 time\, geography\, and cultural context.\n\nAncestral Frequencies: Selecte
 d Works by the MFA Class of 2026 is curated by Annah Lee\, cultural center
  manager for the Town of Holly Springs.\n\nJoin us at the Ackland on Thurs
 day\, April 30\, from 5:30-7:30 p.m.\, for a public opening of the exhibit
 ion. All are welcome.\n\nThis exhibition is made possible by the generous 
 support of Maryanna and Will Johnson.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Ancestral Frequencies: Selected Works by the MFA Class of 2026
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ancestral-frequencies-selected
 -works-by-the-mfa-class-of-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260519T042241Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51375495444252
DTSTART:20260515T160000Z
DTEND:20260515T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:The United Stated Department of the Treasury has proposed a set
  of financial core competencies that will be used to\nestablish a clear un
 derstanding about what all adults should know regarding the basic concepts
  of financial literacy. The\nfive core concept areas identified are:\n• 
 Earning\n• Spending\n• Saving\n• Borrowing\n• Protecting against r
 isk\nThis session covers the basics (or essentials) of each area and descr
 ibes practical skills needed to competently address (or\nmanage) their per
 sonal finances.\n\n \n\nWorkshop Objectives\nAt the end of this workshop\,
  you will be able to:\n• Understand your paycheck in detail\, including 
 its relation to benefits and taxes\n• Develop a spending plan\, track sp
 ending habits\, develop a strategy to live within your means\n• Define a
  personal savings plan\, understand the applicability of different types o
 f financial accounts\, and the personal financial risk associated with sav
 ings and investment vehicles\n• Understand the cost of borrowing and how
  to secure the best types of credit for the need\n• Recognize the need t
 o protect against risk through appropriate insurance vehicles and how to p
 rotect your identity against possible fraud and scams.\n\n \n\nClick on Ca
 rolina Talent registration link and select the “Request” button to aut
 omatically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:The Five Pillars of Personal Finance
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-five-pillars-of-personal-f
 inance-2842
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
